<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27878" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοκός</span></b> , ἡ, later also
			ὁ, <i><span class="en">
			Luc.
			<u>VH</u>
			2.1
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέχομαι</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bearing-beam, main beam,</i> esp.
			in the roof or floor of a house, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.176
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1496
			</span></i>; any <i>balk</i> or <i>beam,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				17.744
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.112
			</span></i>; <i>bar</i> of a gate or door, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				201
			</span></i>: also, in pl., <i>firewood,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PFlor.
				127.5
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>: prov., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ τὴν δοκὸν φέρων</span>”
				<i>one who has 'swallowed a poker',</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1413b28
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν δοκοῖσι</span> is prob. 
				f. l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνδόκοισι</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				66.3
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνδοκος.</span>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> a kind of <i>meteor,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				2.96
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyd.
				<u>Ost.</u>
				10b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοκεύς, δοκίας, δοκίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
